# Security

- Never log API keys, Authorization headers or base64 image payloads.
- Never store provider keys in browser localStorage/sessionStorage.
- Treat Demo paths and player names as untrusted input.
- Canonicalize and validate filesystem paths.
- Use a random analyzer session token.
- Bind analyzer only to loopback.
- Treat CS2 NetCon as a sensitive local attack surface.
- Do not expose a free-form console in production UI.
- Do not implement live competitive information advantage.
- Any feature requiring CS2 injection, memory access or anti-cheat bypass is out of scope.
